## 0.5 Frozen before any strategy is optimised (ADR-0011 §6)

**Hard gates:** fidelity ≤ 0.01% local chord · watertight, conformal interfaces ·
consistent outward normals · surface `min_scaled_jacobian > 0` · deterministic block
count and connectivity · pyHyp completes with zero inverted and zero negative-volume
cells and **min scaled quality strictly > 0** · correct boundary families ·
deterministic cell and block counts · no per-geometry manual repair · confirmed at a
**genuinely finer** level, verified to be finer.

**Ranking:** gates first (failures are *unranked*, not ranked last) → **robustness on
the HOLD-OUT** → worst-case volume quality → cell count → runtime.

**No-winner rule:** if nothing passes every hard gate on every hold-out geometry,
report **no winner**, rank on nearest-miss, and raise it to the user. Fixed now so it
cannot be chosen after seeing results.

`0.30` remains a **ranking target, never a gate.** The hard gate is `> 0`.

**epsE is per-strategy.** `epsE_common_start` is withdrawn as a global constant; it
was calibrated on S1's cell distribution. Ladder `{1.5, 2.0, 3.0}`, never extended
after a failure. S1's own value, carried forward as a starting point: **1.5**.

**Geometry sets:** development on `lhs100_seed42`; **`round_c_lhs10_seed42` is the
hold-out and is still untouched** — `shared/geometry_sets.py` refuses it unless the
caller states the strategy is frozen. `epse_calibration_lhs10_seed7` keeps its role
only as the basis of the recorded Stage 01/02 evidence.

## 0.6 TWO FINDINGS FROM THE MIGRATION

**(a) Instrument bug 7 — the verifier crashed on correctly oriented meshes.**
`tip_edge_nodes` took each OML block's *last j column* as the outboard edge. That
assumes the last column is outboard, and `orient_blocks_consistently` reverses the j
index of every block it flips — seven of eight on `lhs7_00`, including all three OML
blocks. After the orientation fix was wired in, no block matched the tip station and
the check raised `ValueError: need at least one array to concatenate` instead of
returning a result. A flipped strategy would have looked like a **harness crash
rather than a finding**, which is worse than a false failure.

Fixed by applying instrument bug 4's own principle properly: select the tip edge by
spanwise **position**, not by index. This is the **seventh** measurement bug found in
this study's own instruments. `verify the verifier` continues to earn its place in
COMMON_BRIEF.

**(b) S1's frozen Stage 02 configuration does NOT pass the ADR-0011 surface gate.**
The self-test reproduces the recorded numbers exactly — 8 blocks, min scaled Jacobian
**+0.04504** (recorded +0.045), cell-size range **98.83×** (recorded 99×), watertight,
8/8 blocks reached by the orientation walk — and then the surface gate **FAILS** on
one reason:

```
fidelity unverified for spanwise-refined blocks: ['oml_lower', 'oml_upper', 'te_base']
```

`realise_law = True` subdivides between the generator's realised stations, so those
blocks' columns lie *between* stations and cannot be checked against a station
contour. `shared/gates.py` treats **unverified as a failure**, on the grounds that a
gate you did not measure is not a gate you passed.

This is a decision with consequences and it is flagged rather than absorbed:

- The interpolation deviates from the spline loft by **1.99e−02 m ≈ 7.4% of chord**
  against a 0.01%-of-chord hard gate — measured, not assumed (§5B.5).
- cap4 does the same thing (17 native stations refined to 255), so **S0 inherits the
  identical problem**. This is not a penalty aimed at S1.
- But the spanwise law is what made S1 marchable at all: 3462× → 99× cell-size range,
  128/128 bad layers → 0/128 (§5F.2). Turning it off to pass the fidelity gate
  reverts the one thing that worked.

So as things stand, **every strategy that realises a spanwise law fails gate 1, and
every strategy that does not fails to march.** The escape is upstream and is already
identified: have the generator realise more sections, so extra columns lie *on* the
loft instead of on chords of it — `pygeo.extraction.spanwise_sections` is already 25
against the 17 the wing exposes. That is Stage 03 geometry work.

**Open decision for the user.** Three options, none of which should be chosen
silently: (i) do the generator work first, before any strategy is built; (ii) build
the strategies now and carry gate 1 as a known, uniformly-applied failure until the
generator work lands; (iii) amend the gate by ADR to measure fidelity against the
loft rather than against the stations. Recommendation is **(iii) then (i)** —
measuring against the loft is the physically correct instrument and would tell us
whether 7.4% is real or an artefact of comparing against the wrong reference — but
this is a governance change and needs an ADR, not a decision in the moment.

