between the wingtip and the wing." That is ADR-0010, reported by the source, and
reached independently by this study before the thesis was read. §3.1.5 gives the
spanwise law that would fix it (eq 3.5-3.10) and states it is **not used** because
it was never finished; §4.2.3 names the growth limit (1.3-1.6) and states
Openblademesh cannot enforce it. Enforcing it is this study's addition.

**Two constants came from the code listing, not the prose.** "45 degrees" does not
by itself place the outer nose split. Three readings were measured: at the inner
station (vertical connection line, collinear with a near-vertical contour, skew
1.000); solved aft for |dx|=|dz| (-0.816 to -0.902); and the listing's actual rule,
