Openblademesh states and never uses.

**Two hypotheses I held and had to discard, both by measurement:**

* *Cell-size range is the governing metric.* Cutting it 810 -> 173 changed nothing;
  the march still exploded at layer 2. Range is necessary, not sufficient.
* *The narrow min-cell/`s0` spread is what matters.* The constant 0.5 mm edge gave
  the NARROWEST spread (1.29x) and the WORST marching (0/1/4). What predicts passing
  is the absolute VALUE of min-cell/`s0`, not its spread.

The metric that actually found it was the **interface spacing jump** - outboard
spanwise cells of 14-21 mm against tip-cap radial cells of 0.13-1.0 mm, 28:1 across
the tip interface. RUNBOOK §7 Round A lists it as a reported metric and nothing in
this study had been measuring it.

