### S2 BUILT — and it fails the determinism gate (2026-08-15)

ADR-0012 reinstated S2 after finding **both** of ADR-0009's grounds wrong:

* ADR-0009 said the quad-layout-to-structured-block step "does not exist". **It is
  Algorithm 2, printed on p.157 of the paper the strategy is drawn from.**
* ADR-0009 said there was "no concrete route" from available tooling. **gmsh 4.15.2,
  installed throughout, provides `Mesh.Algorithm = 11`** — a cross-field quad mesher.
  `igl`/`QEx`/`meshio`/`shapely` are not needed.

Built to Algorithm 2 and measured on six geometries (tip section, size 0.04c):

| geometry | quads | singularities | blocks |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| 000 / 001 / 002 | 337 / 353 / 287 | 7 / 5 / 6 | **31 / 27 / 37** |
| 003 / 004 / 005 | 347 / 353 / 287 | 7 / 5 / 6 | **39 / 27 / 37** |

**Block count varies 27-39. ADR-0011 §6.1 gate 5 requires a deterministic block
count and connectivity signature; RUNBOOK §2.1 separately disqualifies drifting
connectivity.** S2 fails both.

RUNBOOK §6 S2 named this risk in advance: "Record singularity count and block graph.
**Topology drift across geometries is a production failure.**"

The variation is not noise — geometries 001/004 and 002/005 give identical results
because they share a tip section shape. The block count tracks section shape, and the
design space varies it.

**Two further gate problems found before stopping:** the cap boundary carries 122
nodes against the OML's 61 (all 61 OML nodes survive exactly, but gmsh's pipeline
inserts 61 more — a hanging-node interface pyHyp will not take); and algorithm 8, the
alternative, leaves triangles that Algorithm 2 cannot consume.

**Three readings of "opposite edge of e" were measured**, because the pseudocode is
ambiguous and the difference is enormous: arbitrary-owner gave one 327-quad
mega-block; face-based gave 64-110 blocks; vertex-based — the standard separatrix
definition — gave a credible partition. The first two are recorded because each
looked plausible and would have been reported as a method failure if not checked
against what a partition should look like.

**Stopped here deliberately** (COMMON_BRIEF §4). The cause is identified and no
parameter addresses it: the singularity count is an output of the cross-field solve,
not an input. A deterministic topology needs a constrained cross field with
prescribed singularities — a research component, not a parameter change.

### The fidelity item, now quantified rather than argued

S0 **passes** the surface gate outright at `spanwise_panels=1`. With refinement the
quality is identical (+0.19113) and every station column is still exact, but the
interpolated columns are unverified against the loft. S0 needs the refinement:
unrefined its cell-size range is 517× and aspect ratio 43. So §0.6(b) stands
unchanged as a cross-cutting decision — it is upstream generator work, applies to
cap4 in production, and will apply to every strategy equally.

