# 5E. THE REFRAMING — MARCHABILITY, NOT SHAPE QUALITY (2026-08-13)

## 5E.1 The diagnosis

| | min scaled Jac | cell-size range | min cell / s0 | march |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
| cap4 | **+0.0046** | **153x** | **48.7** | **completes** |
| S1 (as built) | **+0.3250** | 3462x | 0.9 | **explodes at layer 2** |

cap4's cell shape is 70x worse than S1's and it marches. S1's shape is excellent
and it cannot march at all.

March log shows the mechanism: at layer 2 the linear solver hits
`kspMaxIts = 1500`, yields a small negative volume (-9.4e-09), then diverges by
twelve orders of magnitude per layer. **An implicit hyperbolic solve is
conditioned by the RANGE of cell sizes, not by individual cell shape.**

## 5E.2 What was wrong with the whole approach

Stage 02 was spent maximising the minimum scaled Jacobian - the tip-fold hunt
(~15 constructions), the camber-split cap, collar tuning. Every gain came from
**subdividing the tip more finely**, which improves shape and shrinks the
smallest cell. The smallest cell is what breaks the march.

Measured, the two objectives trade monotonically:

| config | range | min scaled Jac |
|---|---:|---:|
| te_base 9, collar 5 | 1068x | +0.3250 |
| te_base 5, collar 3 | 534x | +0.3119 |
| te_base 3, collar 3 | **396x** | +0.1363 |
| cap4 | **153x** | +0.0046 |

Recorded as **ADR-0010**.

## 5E.3 An inconsistency I had introduced

cap4 refines 17 native stations to **255** by linear interpolation. That is
exactly the spanwise law I had disabled on fidelity grounds - so S1 was being
held to a standard the working baseline does not meet. The law is now enabled.
The 7.4%-of-chord interpolation cost is real (an attempt to call it an
over-estimate was itself wrong: the measurement spans two native intervals either
way) and is inherited from cap4's established practice. Removing it for both is
Stage 03 generator work.

