# 5G. TEN-GEOMETRY CALIBRATION + CONFIRMATION (2026-08-14)

## 5G.1 Calibration at `smoke` — 30 marches, all completed

| epsE | passes | note |
|---:|---:|---|
| 1.5 | **10/10** | |
| 2.0 | **10/10** | selected by ADR-0008 (highest passing all ten) |
| 3.0 | 7/10 | fails lhs7_01, lhs7_02, lhs7_08 |

Zero inverted cells anywhere. At epsE 2.0 every geometry gave 0/128 bad layers,
min quality +0.096 to +0.237, all positive. cap4 for comparison: 53/128 bad,
-0.908.

**More dissipation is not monotonically better.** On lhs7_08, epsE 3.0 gives 9
bad layers where 2.0 gives none. Calibrating on lhs7_00 alone - where all three
passed - would have frozen 3.0 and failed three of ten later.

## 5G.2 Confirmation at `fine` — epsE 2.0 FAILS 9/10

| geometry | bad | minQ @ fine | minQ @ smoke |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| lhs7_00 | 0 | +0.251 | +0.234 |
| **lhs7_01** | **1** | **-0.210** | +0.178 |
| lhs7_02 | 0 | +0.062 | +0.205 |
| others | 0 | +0.119 .. +0.250 | - |

**ADR-0008: a value passing at `smoke` and failing at `fine` is NOT selected.**
epsE 2.0 is out. 1.5 cannot be silently substituted - it was only confirmed at
`smoke`, so the ladder is being re-run at `fine`.

This is what the confirmation step is for. Without it, `epsE_common_start = 2.0`
would have been reported as the Stage 02 result and frozen into every downstream
pyHyp strategy.

Refinement is not uniformly harmful: 8 of 10 geometries IMPROVED at `fine`. Two
degraded, one past zero.

## 5G.3 A correction to ADR-0008 itself

The ADR named **L4** as the confirmation level. L4 is N=37 with coarsen=4 -
substantially COARSER than the `smoke` calibration level (N=129, coarsen=1), so
it would have confirmed nothing. Only the coarsen=1 family
(`smoke` -> `fine` -> `production`) is a refinement ladder at full surface
resolution. ADR-0008 and the canary script are corrected; the error is recorded
in the ADR rather than silently patched.

## 5G.4 NEGATIVE RESULT — no surface metric predicts this failure

Three hypotheses tested against the lhs7_01 failure, none holds:

| hypothesis | evidence against |
|---|---|
| cell-size range | lhs7_01 has the **second-best** range (88x); the worst (190x, lhs7_07) passes |
| max adjacent normal angle | lhs7_01 is 26.74 deg, mid-range of the passers (26.6-34.0) |
| twist reversal | lhs7_03 and lhs7_04 also reverse twist and both pass |

The bad cell is at **layer 0, the first cell off the wall**, with POSITIVE volume
(7.97e-11) and negative quality (-0.210).

**Cell-size range predicts catastrophic explosion; it does not predict marginal
single-layer failure.** That is a real limit on the ADR-0010 marchability model
and is recorded rather than papered over with a fourth story.

## 5G.5 Running

epsE 1.5 and 3.0 at `fine` on all ten (20 marches). Selection will be the highest
value passing all ten **at `fine`**. If none passes all ten, ADR-0008 section 6
applies: stop and report, do not extend the ladder.

